# {{.ServiceName}}

Generated with KPro's `http-api` project profile. The service starts from
`cmd/{{.ServiceName}}`, keeps the application-owned API implementation in
`internal/api/service`, and derives checked HTTP bindings from
`api/openapi.yaml`.

```bash
go mod tidy
go run ./cmd/{{.ServiceName}}
```

After changing the OpenAPI contract, regenerate and verify the checked-in
outputs:

```bash
kpro generate
kpro generate --check
```

Generated files are replaced only while they still match the generation lock;
the service implementation is create-once and remains safe to edit. The starter
server also sets explicit request timeouts and 1 MiB header/body limits. Adjust
those values and application configuration for the target workload.
